                            {
                                "target_word": "foil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "179fd008-1c09-3034-86ef-a2626f3c5942",
                                        "entry_id": "520d00f8-79a7-3a79-afdc-d688f6c78c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prevent (something) from being accomplished."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2151856e-4588-4d2d-b604-7b3f23ec3187",
                                                "sense_id": "179fd008-1c09-3034-86ef-a2626f3c5942",
                                                "text": "They foiled my plans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                        "entry_id": "520d00f8-79a7-3a79-afdc-d688f6c78c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prevent (someone) from accomplishing something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c87df181-6fd0-4a89-9156-11e49846b25f",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "I was foiled by my superior"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecd27c7b-eae3-43e5-90ed-0d7651fa2fa6",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "And at the field fought before Bebriacum, ere the battailes joyned, tvvo Ægles had a conflict and bickered together in all their fights: and vvhen the one of them was foyled and overcome, a third came at the very inſtant from the ſunne riſing and chaſed the Victreſſe avvay."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14564b1f-6790-43d7-ad9c-d572611af301",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "And by mortal man at length am foil'd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c082237c-71c2-4d6f-b800-16699714a9d7",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "her long locks that foil the painter's power"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc57a0e3-6d2f-4c11-8b47-15463f64e3e7",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "Perhaps you think you love me now but it is only for an instant, and because you are foiled."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fee37603-6df0-49f8-b15c-a5c1d92a46ad",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "First, former Toffee Mikel Arteta sent Walcott racing clear but instead of shooting he squared towards Ramsey, who was foiled by Tony Hibbert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ac89d65-1d71-4c91-a669-3fbdbbd5f620",
                                                "sense_id": "f1ff6fd3-595a-3a51-9d45-f19c8a0c73e6",
                                                "text": "Many jihadist plots have been foiled and the security apparatus is getting better, overall, at pre-empting those who would do us ill. But, they say, the nature of the threat and the terrorists’ increasing use of low-tech, asymmetrical tactics such as hire vehicles and knives, make it all but impossible to stop every assault."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82908fda-6921-3936-a0eb-08d525833f19",
                                        "entry_id": "520d00f8-79a7-3a79-afdc-d688f6c78c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To blunt; to dull; to spoil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6288468e-0034-4093-8f61-91251ad9a55b",
                                                "sense_id": "82908fda-6921-3936-a0eb-08d525833f19",
                                                "text": "they foil the scent of one another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0fda7949-b4d5-3de7-a081-80fe3e6de079",
                                        "entry_id": "520d00f8-79a7-3a79-afdc-d688f6c78c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tread underfoot; to trample."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c7a687e-cbc6-4e1a-9829-5c2ed44f3f26",
                                                "sense_id": "0fda7949-b4d5-3de7-a081-80fe3e6de079",
                                                "text": "King Richard […] caused the ensigns of Leopold to be pulled down and foiled underfoot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc02ab94-562d-4258-9766-970d9d1bc5d7",
                                                "sense_id": "0fda7949-b4d5-3de7-a081-80fe3e6de079",
                                                "text": "Whom he did all to pieces breake and foyle, / In filthy durt, and left so in the loathely soyle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
